at's partly because  village populations have been declining  for decades  do people live in all of these homes as  locals sell or abandon their homes to  seek jobs in cities like rome and milan  says mayor domenico credico the tourists  who come here stay in apartments  restored by the town  luring them here with free vacations has  been a spectacular success for such a  tiny hamlet  so 8 000 people requested to come here  but mass tourism isn't what they're  after he says  in the age of covet 19 a lack of crowds  is its own  attraction as are the friendships that  can only be formed on an  intimate scale the main reason this  couple says  they can't wait to come back one  very important thing in melisa  that you can't  every day find in other regions  these people people here is really  special real wonderful  now of course getting here is still a  challenge with that eu  travel ban still in place on americans  fortunately  the town says as soon as it's lifted  americans are  more than welcome to have their free  vacation here too  for cbs this morning saturday chris  livesay molise  italy sign me i think we're all in  anywhere in italy as soon as possible  would be wonderful with sheep intestines  maybe maybe not how's your stomach doing  it's better good  all right there's your update from  michelle
 

